description:
A synthetic 3D benchmark function with a modified Rosenbrock term, fractional power terms for non-separability, and an asymmetric exponential term for skewness.

f(x) = sum( (1-x[i])**2 + 100*(x[i+1] - x[i]**2)**2 )  + 0.2*sum(abs(x)**0.7) + 0.6 * exp((sum(x) + 1.5*x[0] - 0.5*x[1])/4)

The Rosenbrock part provides a basic difficult landscape, with the modification that involves interaction with other dimensions;
The fractional powers add increased non-separability and ruggedness;
The exponential term induces skewness.
